{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'tools/protocol.py' -Encoding UTF8 -TotalCount 55; \"'$p='\"'tools/protocol.py'; \"'$s=Get-Content -LiteralPath $p -Encoding UTF8; 180..245 | ForEach-Object { '\"'{0}:{1}' -f (\"'$_+1),$s[$_] }'","aggregated_output":"r\"\"\"protocol.py - the session protocol v1 core (docs/session-protocol.md, APPROVED by the user 2026-09-24:\r\n\"통신 규약은 … 모든 영역에 JSON 적용하도록 하고 … 목표지도 … 규약 필드 추가 … 사용자 결정도 이렇게 구현하여 적용하도록 하자\").\r\n\r\nSTANDARD LIBRARY ONLY. No LabVIEW, no network.\r\n\r\nWHAT EXISTED BEFORE THIS FILE (checked first, CLAUDE.md \"check what exists\"): no validator, no `docs/protocol/`, no\r\n`tools/bench/cards/`. The log verdict lived as FOUR different text scans - `bgrun.inner_re`, `guard_peer.FAILURE_RE`,\r\n`audit_cycle.FAILURE_RE`, `cycle_runner.GATE_FAIL_RE` - which drifted apart and read quoted prose as failures\r\n(cycles 70, 71, 73). This module replaces them with ONE reading of ONE line (C6).\r\n\r\nCLI\r\n    py tools/protocol.py validate <card.json>              exit 0 \"OK <schema>\" | exit 1 \"INVALID <reason>\"\r\n    py tools/protocol.py new <kind> --id 74-03 [--force]   skeleton card -> tools/bench/cards/<kind>_<id>.json\r\n    py tools/protocol.py result-line --pass N --fail M [--first-fail TEXT] [--artefact PATH ...]\r\n    py tools/protocol.py verdict <log>                     the C6 verdict of the log's LAST run (JSON)\r\n    py tools/protocol.py bind <task-card>                  C2: a card agent's FIRST command (the hook records it)\r\n    py tools/protocol.py parse-verdict <answer> [--id X] [--out cards/verdict_X.json]    C5\r\n    py tools/protocol.py render-review <review-card>       C4: the card block + verdict contract peer.ps1 sends\r\n\r\nIMPORTABLE\r\n    load_card(path) -> dict           (raises ValueError(reason) when invalid)\r\n    validate_obj(obj, goal_ids=None) -> (ok, reason)\r\n    result_line(d) -> \"RESULT {...}\"  (validated result-line/1)\r\n    parse_result_line(text) -> dict | None      the LAST `RESULT {` line of the text (malformed -> a FAIL dict)\r\n    run_verdict(segment) / log_verdict(text, legacy_re=None, mtime=None) / first_fail_signature(segment, ...)\r\n\r\nTHE SWITCH (history is not rewritten): a bgrun run segment that carries a RESULT line is judged by it. A segment\r\nWITHOUT one is judged by its exit code alone (`BGRUN END rc=` / `BGRUN TIMEOUT`) - EXCEPT when that run STARTED\r\nbefore SWITCH_TS, in which case the caller's OLD text rule (`legacy_re`) still applies, so every historical verdict\r\nstays what it was.\r\n\r\nAGGREGATION, stated because the draft says \"the LAST RESULT line\": `parse_result_line` returns the last one, but a run\r\nVERDICT fails when ANY RESULT line printed by that run fails. Reason: a chained command (`motor_gate ...; motor_gate\r\n...`, tools/bench/pi_testmove_20260923e.log) prints one RESULT per step, and the last step passing must not hide an\r\nearlier rejected move. For a single script (stagekit) the two readings coincide: failures only accumulate.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport io\r\nimport json\r\nimport os\r\nimport re\r\nimport sys\r\nimport time\r\n\r\ntry:\r\n    sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\r\nexcept Exception:                                                                   # noqa: BLE001\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\r\nROOT = os.path.dirname(HERE)\r\nSCHEMA_DIR = os.path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"protocol\")\r\nCARDS_DIR = os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\", \"cards\")\r\nGOALMAP = os.path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"goalmap.json\")\r\n\r\n181:def validate_obj(obj, goal_ids=None):\r\n182:    \"\"\"(True, 'OK <schema>') or (False, '<one-line reason>'). `goal_ids`: when given, every advances/unblocks/blocks\r\n183:    id must be one of them (the CLI passes docs/goalmap.json's ids; the self-test passes a fixture).\"\"\"\r\n184:    if not isinstance(obj, dict):\r\n185:        return False, \"top level is %s, not a JSON object\" % type(obj).__name__\r\n186:    try:\r\n187:        schema = load_schema(obj.get(\"schema\"))\r\n188:    except ValueError as e:\r\n189:        return False, str(e)\r\n190:    err = _check(obj, schema, schema, \"$\")\r\n191:    if err:\r\n192:        return False, err\r\n193:    if goal_ids is not None:\r\n194:        cited = (list(obj.get(\"advances\") or []) + ([obj[\"unblocks\"]] if obj.get(\"unblocks\") else [])\r\n195:                 + list(obj.get(\"goal_ids\") or []))                                     # steer/1\r\n196:\r\n197:        for it in obj.get(\"items\") or []:\r\n198:            if isinstance(it, dict):\r\n199:                cited += list(it.get(\"blocks\") or [])\r\n200:        unknown = sorted(set(cited) - set(goal_ids))\r\n201:        if unknown:\r\n202:            return False, \"$: goal-map id(s) %s not in docs/goalmap.json\" % unknown\r\n203:    return True, \"OK \" + obj[\"schema\"]\r\n204:\r\n205:\r\n206:def load_card(path, goal_ids=None):\r\n207:    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\r\n208:        try:\r\n209:            obj = json.load(f)\r\n210:        except ValueError as e:\r\n211:            raise ValueError(\"not JSON: %s\" % e)\r\n212:    ok, why = validate_obj(obj, goal_ids)\r\n213:    if not ok:\r\n214:        raise ValueError(why)\r\n215:    return obj\r\n216:\r\n217:\r\n218:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- C6 RESULT line\r\n219:def result_line(d):\r\n220:    \"\"\"The one-line text form. Validated; ASCII-escaped so a cp949 console can always print it.\"\"\"\r\n221:    d = dict(d)\r\n222:    d.setdefault(\"schema\", \"result-line/1\")\r\n223:    ok, why = validate_obj(d)\r\n224:    if not ok:\r\n225:        raise ValueError(\"result_line: \" + why)\r\n226:    return RESULT_PREFIX + json.dumps(d, ensure_ascii=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\r\n227:\r\n228:\r\n229:def make_result(n_pass, n_fail, first_fail=None, artefacts=(), status=None):\r\n230:    st = status or (\"PASS\" if (n_fail == 0 and not first_fail) else \"FAIL\")\r\n231:    ff = None if first_fail is None else str(first_fail)[:200]\r\n232:    return {\"schema\": \"result-line/1\", \"status\": st, \"gates\": {\"pass\": int(n_pass), \"fail\": int(n_fail)},\r\n233:            \"first_fail\": ff, \"artefacts\": list(artefacts)}\r\n234:\r\n235:\r\n236:def _malformed(raw, why):\r\n237:    return {\"schema\": \"result-line/1\", \"status\": \"FAIL\", \"gates\": {\"pass\": 0, \"fail\": 1},\r\n238:            \"first_fail\": (\"malformed RESULT line (%s): %s\" % (why, raw))[:200], \"artefacts\": []}\r\n239:\r\n240:\r\n241:def all_result_lines(text):\r\n242:    out = []\r\n243:    for m in RESULT_LINE_RE.finditer(text or \"\"):\r\n244:        raw = m.group(1)\r\n245:        try:\r\n246:            d = json.loads(raw)\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
